1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,709
A bowling ball rolls down a lane.

2
00:00:02,709 --> 00:00:04,617
A coin rolls off the table.

3
00:00:04,617 --> 00:00:06,476
A ring rolls down a slope.

4
00:00:06,876 --> 00:00:10,998
They all start from rest, but they
do not all roll at the same speed.

5
00:00:11,448 --> 00:00:15,117
Diya lets a ring, a disc and a ball
go from the same height on the same

6
00:00:15,117 --> 00:00:16,017
slope.

7
00:00:15,941 --> 00:00:17,615
Same start, same slope.

8
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:21,186
Yet the ball wins and the
ring comes last, every time.

9
00:00:21,186 --> 00:00:22,086
Why?

10
00:00:22,176 --> 00:00:24,931
The answer is hidden in
the energy of rolling.

11
00:00:25,531 --> 00:00:28,112
A rolling body does two things at once.

12
00:00:28,112 --> 00:00:30,289
It moves forward, and it spins.

13
00:00:30,639 --> 00:00:33,322
So it has two kinds of kinetic energy.

14
00:00:33,322 --> 00:00:36,260
One half m v squared, for moving forward.

15
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:39,502
And one half I omega
squared, for spinning.

16
00:00:39,502 --> 00:00:42,116
Its total energy is the sum of the two.

17
00:00:42,516 --> 00:00:45,085
Note: rolling is not in
the current NCERT book.

18
00:00:45,085 --> 00:00:47,004
It is in the JEE Advanced syllabus.

19
00:00:47,604 --> 00:00:48,889
Our motion notebook.

20
00:00:48,889 --> 00:00:52,305
A thirty degree slope, two
metres long, one metre high.

21
00:00:52,305 --> 00:00:54,166
A ring, a disc and a ball.

22
00:00:54,516 --> 00:00:55,434
Let them go.

23
00:00:55,434 --> 00:00:57,726
The ball pulls ahead, then the disc.

24
00:00:57,726 --> 00:00:58,920
The ring is last.

25
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:02,201
On the graph, each speed
grows in a straight line.

26
00:01:02,201 --> 00:01:04,004
The ball's line is the steepest.

27
00:01:04,404 --> 00:01:08,735
At the bottom: the ball moves at three
point seven four metres per second,

28
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:13,076
the disc at three point six two, and
the ring at three point one three.

29
00:01:13,576 --> 00:01:14,494
Slow-mo replay.

30
00:01:14,494 --> 00:01:16,485
Freeze in the middle of the race.

31
00:01:16,835 --> 00:01:18,540
Look at the energy bars.

32
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:22,906
Each body turned the same height into
energy, but split it in different

33
00:01:22,906 --> 00:01:23,806
ways.

34
00:01:23,851 --> 00:01:26,567
The ring puts half of
its energy into spinning.

35
00:01:26,567 --> 00:01:28,081
The disc puts one third.

36
00:01:28,081 --> 00:01:29,854
The ball, only two sevenths.

37
00:01:30,254 --> 00:01:34,030
Less energy spent on spinning
means more for moving forward.

38
00:01:34,030 --> 00:01:35,845
So the ball moves fastest.

39
00:01:36,445 --> 00:01:37,400
Now you try.

40
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:41,660
A heavy disc and a light disc, the
same size, race down the slope.

41
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:42,755
Which one wins?

42
00:01:42,755 --> 00:01:43,943
Pause and decide.

43
00:01:47,043 --> 00:01:47,988
It is a tie!

44
00:01:47,988 --> 00:01:49,097
Mass cancels out.

45
00:01:49,097 --> 00:01:51,057
Only the shape decides the speed.

46
00:01:51,657 --> 00:01:53,362
Why does the ring lose?

47
00:01:53,362 --> 00:01:54,445
Link by link.

48
00:01:54,795 --> 00:01:58,219
All of the ring's mass sits
at the rim, far from the axis.

49
00:01:58,619 --> 00:02:01,790
Mass far from the axis makes
spinning cost more energy.

50
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:06,359
So the ring spends the biggest share
on spin, and has the least left for

51
00:02:06,359 --> 00:02:07,259
speed.

52
00:02:07,506 --> 00:02:09,598
Now the rule, one step at a time.

53
00:02:09,948 --> 00:02:10,848
Step one.

54
00:02:10,804 --> 00:02:15,599
Total energy is one half m v squared,
plus one half I omega squared.

55
00:02:16,349 --> 00:02:17,249
Step two.

56
00:02:17,243 --> 00:02:21,592
Put omega equal to v over R,
and I equal to m k squared.

57
00:02:21,592 --> 00:02:26,824
K equals one half m v squared, times
one plus k squared over R squared.

58
00:02:27,574 --> 00:02:28,490
Step three.

59
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:32,335
The bottom point does not
slip, so friction does no work.

60
00:02:32,335 --> 00:02:34,397
So m g h equals that energy.

61
00:02:35,147 --> 00:02:36,096
Step four.

62
00:02:36,096 --> 00:02:41,000
v equals root of two g h, over
one plus k squared over R squared.

63
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,395
The mass cancels.

64
00:02:43,145 --> 00:02:44,045
Step five.

65
00:02:44,002 --> 00:02:47,104
For a ring, k squared
over R squared is one.

66
00:02:47,104 --> 00:02:48,680
For a disc, a half.

67
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:50,453
For a ball, two fifths.

68
00:02:50,453 --> 00:02:52,117
The smallest value wins.

69
00:02:52,867 --> 00:02:53,840
Remember this.

70
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:57,386
A rolling body shares its energy
between moving and spinning.

71
00:02:57,386 --> 00:02:59,868
The less it spins, the faster it goes.

72
00:03:00,568 --> 00:03:01,650
Side by side.

73
00:03:01,650 --> 00:03:05,936
A rolling ball must spin, so part
of its energy goes into spin.

74
00:03:06,336 --> 00:03:09,423
A block slides down a smooth
slope of the same height.

75
00:03:09,423 --> 00:03:10,970
It does not spin at all.

76
00:03:11,570 --> 00:03:12,516
Now you try.

77
00:03:12,516 --> 00:03:16,848
Which reaches the bottom first: the
rolling ball, or the sliding block?

78
00:03:16,848 --> 00:03:18,022
Pause and decide.

79
00:03:21,222 --> 00:03:22,404
The sliding block!

80
00:03:22,404 --> 00:03:26,162
None of its energy goes into
spin, so all of it becomes speed.

81
00:03:26,162 --> 00:03:28,534
Four point four three metres per second.

82
00:03:29,184 --> 00:03:30,875
Now, one worked example.

83
00:03:31,225 --> 00:03:35,629
A solid ball of mass two kilograms
rolls without slipping at three metres

84
00:03:35,629 --> 00:03:36,534
per second.

85
00:03:36,534 --> 00:03:40,329
Find its total kinetic energy,
and the part that is spin.

86
00:03:40,829 --> 00:03:44,598
Moving forward: one half
times two times three squared.

87
00:03:44,598 --> 00:03:45,602
Nine joules.

88
00:03:46,352 --> 00:03:50,210
For a solid ball, k squared
over R squared is two fifths.

89
00:03:50,210 --> 00:03:52,345
So spin is two fifths of nine.

90
00:03:52,345 --> 00:03:53,959
Three point six joules.

91
00:03:54,709 --> 00:03:57,031
Total: nine plus three point six.

92
00:03:57,031 --> 00:03:58,693
Twelve point six joules.

93
00:03:59,343 --> 00:04:00,805
Now, the exam trap.

94
00:04:01,155 --> 00:04:05,225
Many students think friction on a
rolling body wastes energy, like on a

95
00:04:05,225 --> 00:04:06,125
sliding one.

96
00:04:06,506 --> 00:04:10,260
In rolling without slipping,
the contact point is at rest.

97
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,015
So friction does no work.

98
00:04:12,015 --> 00:04:15,271
It only moves energy from
forward motion into spin.

99
00:04:15,921 --> 00:04:17,418
Where is this asked?

100
00:04:17,418 --> 00:04:22,380
In races down a slope, energy shares,
and how high a rolling body climbs.

101
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:24,092
Exam level now.

102
00:04:24,092 --> 00:04:28,118
A solid cylinder rolls without
slipping towards a slope at four metres

103
00:04:28,118 --> 00:04:29,018
per second.

104
00:04:28,986 --> 00:04:29,886
g is ten.

105
00:04:29,815 --> 00:04:32,200
How high up the slope does it climb?

106
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,360
Pause and solve.

107
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,140
The answer is B.

108
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:41,788
One point two metres.

109
00:04:42,288 --> 00:04:46,232
For a solid cylinder, k squared
over R squared is one half.

110
00:04:46,732 --> 00:04:51,853
Energy: one half m v squared,
times one point five, equals m g h.

111
00:04:51,853 --> 00:04:53,265
The mass cancels.

112
00:04:53,765 --> 00:04:57,521
So h equals sixteen times
one point five, over twenty.

113
00:04:57,521 --> 00:04:59,106
One point two metres.

114
00:04:59,706 --> 00:05:01,246
Here is your recap.

115
00:05:01,246 --> 00:05:02,829
Screenshot this card.

116
00:05:06,029 --> 00:05:07,968
Can you answer these without help?

117
00:05:08,368 --> 00:05:09,268
One.

118
00:05:08,790 --> 00:05:11,104
Why does the ring come last in the race?

119
00:05:12,004 --> 00:05:12,904
Two.

120
00:05:12,425 --> 00:05:15,724
Why do a heavy disc and a light
disc of the same size tie?

121
00:05:16,624 --> 00:05:17,524
Three.

122
00:05:17,137 --> 00:05:20,818
Why does friction do no work on a
body that rolls without slipping?

123
00:05:21,718 --> 00:05:25,570
Next chapter: why do the planets move
faster when they come closer to the

124
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:26,470
Sun?

125
00:05:25,994 --> 00:05:28,194
Gravitation, starting with Kepler's laws.
